        "Sit on the left hip with both feet out to the right side, and rest the hands on the thighs with the fingers together." to "Zauna a kan kwatangwalo na hagu tare da ƙafafu biyu zuwa gefen dama, kuma ku kwantar da hannaye a kan cinyoyin tare da yatsunsu tare.",
        "At ‘ash-hadu al-la ilaha’ raise the index finger of the right hand, and lower it at ‘illallah’." to "A ‘ash-hadu al-la ilaha’ ka daga yatsan hannun dama, ka runtse shi zuwa ‘illallah’.",
        "These steps follow the Hanafi method. In the Shafi‘i school: the hands are folded above the navel; the opening dua is ‘Wajjahtu wajhiya…’; Bismillah is recited as part of al-Fatihah and Ameen is said aloud in the loud prayers; the hands are raised when going into ruku‘ and when rising from it; the follower also recites al-Fatihah; and Qunut is read in Fajr after the ruku‘ of the second rak‘ah. Learn the details from a teacher of your school." to "Wadannan matakan suna bin hanyar Hanafiyya. A cikin mazhabar Shafi’i: Hannu suna nade sama da cibiya; addu’ar budewa ita ce ‘Wajjahtu wajhiya…’; Ana karanta Bismillah a cikin fatiha kuma ana yin addu'a da babbar murya Ameen; ana daga hannaye yayin shiga ruku’i da lokacin dagowa daga gare ta; mai bi kuma ya karanta fatiha; kuma ana karanta Qunut a cikin Fajr bayan ruku’i na raka’a ta biyu. Koyi cikakken bayani daga malamin makarantar ku.",
        "These steps follow the Hanafi method. In the Maliki school: the arms are commonly left at the sides; no opening dua, Ta‘awwuz or Bismillah is recited in a Fard prayer; the follower does not recite behind the imam in the loud prayers; Qunut is read quietly in Fajr; and the prayer is ended with one obligatory salam. Learn the details from a teacher of your school." to "Wadannan matakan suna bin hanyar Hanafiyya. A cikin mazhabar Malikiyya: an fi barin hannaye a gefe; ba a karanta dua, Ta’awwuz ko Bismillah a cikin addu’ar Fardi; mabiyi baya karantawa a bayan liman a cikin babbar sallah; Ana karanta Qunut cikin nutsuwa a cikin Fajr; kuma ana idar da sallah da sallama guda daya. Koyi cikakken bayani daga malamin makarantar ku.",
        "These steps follow the Hanafi method. In the Hanbali school: the same Thana is recited; Ameen is said aloud in the loud prayers; the hands are raised when going into ruku‘ and when rising from it; ‘Rabbighfir li’ between the two sajdahs is required; and Witr is commonly prayed as two rak‘at and then one, with Qunut after ruku‘. Learn the details from a teacher of your school." to "Wadannan matakan suna bin hanyar Hanafiyya. A mazhabar Hanbali: Haka ake karantawa Thana; Ameen yana daga murya a cikin babbar sallah; ana daga hannaye yayin shiga ruku’i da lokacin dagowa daga gare ta; ‘Rabbighfir li’ a tsakanin sajdah biyu ana buqatar; kuma ana yawaita yin sallar witr raka’a biyu sannan a yi sallah daya, da Qunut bayan ruku’i. Koyi cikakken bayani daga malamin makarantar ku.",
        "Before you begin" to "Kafin ka fara",
